    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "The Namib Desert relief is characterized by an immense, seemingly endless sea of shifting sand dunes that run parallel to the harsh Atlantic coastline. This hyper-arid coastal desert stretches for over 2,000 kilometers and is defined by extreme geographical extremes, from the towering 300-meter-high red dunes of Sossusvlei in the south to the flat, barren gravel plains of the Skeleton Coast in the north. The entire relief is heavily shaped by the persistent, powerful south-westerly winds that constantly reshape the dunes, creating a highly dynamic, ever-changing landscape. Earth Science K6 — aeolian landforms."
